],[680.0,-0.7445],[685.0,-1.0238],[690.0,-1.0238]]},"source":{"document":"E-4024","date":"2005-09","file":"kodak-e100g.pdf","url":"https://125px.com/docs/film/kodak/e4024-Ektachrome_E100G.pdf","sha256":"9eaa5bd754a77c3d12b4b268e934361df53f54bdf83304f3653d1514904a5e76"},"notes":["Shared datasheet E-4024 for E100G and E100GX: each film has its own characteristic curves; the spectral-sensitivity and spectral-dye-density plots are printed once for both films ('E100G and E100GX Films'), so the sensitivity and dyes traced here are the same in both sheets.","Characteristic curves (E100G plot, upper left of printed page 5): x axis is absolute log exposure in lux-seconds (daylight, 1/100 s), as printed; density falls with exposure (reversal film). On the sheet B is the highest curve, G the middle, R the lowest.","Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 1/10 second, process E-6, density E.N.D. = 1.0 (equivalent neutral density); y is log sensitivity (reciprocal exposure in erg/cm2 required to produce the specified density) as printed. The low tails are drawn only part-way down on the sheet.","Spectral dye density: dyes normalized to form a visual neutral density of 1.0 for a 5000 K viewing illuminant, process E-6; diffuse spectral density. The unlabelled top curve is the sum of the three dyes and is traced as 'neutral'. No separate minimum-density curve is plotted.","Grain: diffuse rms granularity 8 (extremely fine), read at a gross diffuse visual density of 1.0 with a 48-micrometre aperture (both films). Exposure index 100 for daylight or electronic flash; 3200 K tungsten with 80A filter EI 25.","E100G has a neutral colour balance."],"dyes":{"y":[[400.0,0.5219],[405.0,0.5612],[410.0,0.6272],[415.0,0.6932],[420.0,0.7575],[425.0,0.8126],[430.0,0.8562],[435.0,0.8897],[440.0,0.9156],[445.0,0.9281],[450.0,0.9188],[455.0,0.9052],[460.0,0.8768],[465.0,0.8253],[470.0,0.7598],[475.0,0.6892],[480.0,0.6182],[485.0,0.5447],[490.0,0.469],[495.0,0.3922],[500.0,0.326],[505.0,0.2667],[510.